{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas","id":1189336,"title":"Are \u00c6on Abberants still comparable to Novas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-24T20:10:43-08:00","id":1189336,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Are \u00c6on Abberants still comparable to Novas?","content":"So still new to the setting but the forums always gave me the impression that Aberrants were not comparable to the Novas in personal Puissance. They emphasized they were inhuman mutants, seemed to be the implication of superevolved humans breeding with each other becoming less human and maybe each generation/individual its own separate species. But that they were superhuman, but not gonzo level, and had insane tech because they didn't have the universal censoring of Reed Richards level tech Earth had.<br /> <br /> But is it true? What are examples of Aberrant powerlevels? Did Novas always produce Nova Children, even with humans? And do they have any estimate at all of Aberrant populations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T22:37:50-08:00","id":1189348,"title":"","content":"In the Aeon time period there are two types of entities called Aberrants, those that would be called Novas, and creatures mutated by more alien Novas to serve them(kind of like Ghouls in vampire!). From a mechanical standpoint the term is also used for Tier 4 Novas.<br /> <br /> Subaberrant mutants are obviously less powerful than Novas. Novas of a similar Quantum level will be roughly the same power level as more mutated versions but since taint had previously allowed one to buy powers cheaper the more taint you have the more you can cheat that scenario. Tier 4 characters are obviously more powerful than Tier 3, they have easier dice rolls higher caps on stat and insane powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nova Fertility is... unknown, in previous editions there was an elaborate conspiracy to sterilize them but they also seemed to be naturally of lower fertility. Generally Nova/baseline breeding would lead to a baseline but.. there were ways to make baselines unnaturally errupt in previous editions too so its complicated and since we don't have Aberrant yet for 2e we really don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T22:46:48-08:00","id":1189352,"title":"","content":"I see. What do you mean by unnaturally errupt?<br /> <br /> So the populations of the space Aberrants like in Eden would mostly be derived from human stock what kidnapped when they left earth? Are mutated human style novas at least able to birth or is it assumed they breed them and novify them later, ala Inhumans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T01:12:39-08:00","id":1189363,"title":"","content":"The Humans of Eden likely were not kidnapped by the Novas that originally settled the planet, but were likely the friends, family and colleagues that voluntarily joined this group when they left Earth at the end of the Aberrant War. The Novas that protect them do not show any signs of the quantum corruption that pushed many Novas to become inhuman Aberrants (at least not that we have yet seen).<br /> <br /> As for the other Aberrants that have been encountered, the ones that are actively attacking Earth installations... these mutants are very high with the quantum corruption that have made them very inhuman... possibly beyond the ability to procreate in any understandable fashion we would recognize. When these Aberrants use their corrupted powers, they leave the area saturated (to various degrees) with corrupted quantum energy that can turn baseline humans into sub-Aberrant mutants. These mutants, with enough exposure to the corrupted quantum energy that transformed them could become full Aberrants with corrupted quantum powers. This may not be procreation as we would understand it, but it does allow the Aberrants to increase their numbers dramatically over time (the greater the corruption they cause, the quicker the transformation). At least this is the way it appears to be with the new setting, but I will admit that we don't have all the information to confirm this just yet (but it does seem likely in my &quot;non-expert&quot; opinion)<br /> <br /> As for unnaturally erupting... the powers of Novas and Aberrants (and the Stalwarts that proceeded them) are the rarest of the three types (Talents and Psiads) to develop naturally (as in without any outside influence other that the possible ). There were methods to cause others to gain these same powers through artificial means rather than let them develop naturally. Even the process that Aeon Aberrants seem to be using to create more of their can by turning humans into sub-Aberrant mutants is an artificial means of bringing out such powers.<br /> <br /> Speaking of artificial means... it could be said that the Psions of the Aeon setting are receiving their powers through artificial means too... as Psiads are the ones that develop their powers naturally, while the Prometheus Chambers artificially enhance a Latent's psychic potential... even overwriting it in favor of a specific aptitude. Doesn't exactly sound &quot;natural&quot; now, does it? Makes you wonder if the Orders really are that different from the Aberrants they are fighting, does it not? Okay, maybe they do give you a choice to remain Latent or become a Psion... but is it really a choice if one's options are rather limited if one doesn't take the opportunity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T07:33:11-08:00","id":1189395,"title":"","content":"When the Antagonists chapter gets previewed, you'll have mechanics and stats and such for a variety of levels of aberrants, from hordes of mutants (normal people or animals who were changed into footsoldiers by a true aberrant or Corrupted Zone) all the way up to major threats that will require a team armed with psi powers and fancy tech to defeat. You can use those rules to fake an Edenite nova, too, until _Aberrant_ is written and we have a better approximation.<br /> <br /> The Edenites from the new edition are presented as somewhat less overwhelmingly powerful than the ones from 1st edition, deliberately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T07:58:02-08:00","id":1189398,"title":"","content":"But the Edenites are full on Novas, with all the natural traits and powers of Novas and should be at that level. <br /> <br /> I hope this is simply a Trinity treatment rather than a statement that Novas have lost some of there power levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T08:19:00-08:00","id":1189402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1189398#post1189398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Edenites are full on Novas, with all the natural traits and powers of Novas and should be at that level.<br /> <br /> I hope this is simply a Trinity treatment rather than a statement that Novas have lost some of there power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have absolutely no idea what PC novas will look like...that game hasn't been written yet.<br /> <br /> What I can say is that moving the Karroo Incident away from &quot;Apollo Milliken waves his hand and vaporizes an entire alien fleet&quot; and toward &quot;it was a real fight, with Edenites and Karroo colonists and Upeo psions all working together&quot; was a directive that came from over my pay grade, and one that I happily agreed with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T08:25:56-08:00","id":1189403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1189398#post1189398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Edenites are full on Novas, with all the natural traits and powers of Novas and should be at that level.<br /> <br /> I hope this is simply a Trinity treatment rather than a statement that Novas have lost some of there power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>First ed Edenites were ludicrously powerful, even for Novas, weren't they? When a single one is blowing up a &quot;massive&quot; fleet of spaceships, they're well beyond anything we actually saw canon Aberrant-era Novas do. It's the higher end of even the Player's Guide material, IIRC. Not quite Quantum Inferno, but way beyond anything even Quantum 6 could do.<br /> <br /> Eden doesn't appear to be the home of Quantum 8 Novas, because at that point, they're capable doing things like redesigning a planet to fit their will with complete mastery over climate, geology and life itself, granting mental and social Mega-Attributes to entire populations, turning baselines into Novas (And boosting the powers of other Novas) and travelling through time. Frankly, anything less than utter post-scarcity paradise, populated by post-humans with super intelligence and charisma, free of the little things like ageing and illness, is an utter failure of the ruling class. And that's not Eden as it's presented. It's just a pretty nice place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T08:35:27-08:00","id":1189406,"title":"","content":"Nod. Nod. Okay all, very good points. Thanks for providing them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T13:25:43-08:00","id":1189453,"title":"","content":"Besides, it's always easier to start off with someone weaker and go &quot;oh they just weren't as powerful as our PCs, and haven't grown into their power yet&quot; if we've changed our mind by the time we get to the nova rules that are supposed to govern them. It's much harder to give them god-like power now and then change our minds later.<br /> <br /> The new presentation of Edenites works better for Aeon and it works better for Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T17:52:27-08:00","id":1189499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1189352#post1189352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. What do you mean by unnaturally errupt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Higher levels of certain powers would allow even people without MR nodes to Errupt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the populations of the space Aberrants like in Eden would mostly be derived from human stock what kidnapped when they left earth? Are mutated human style novas at least able to birth or is it assumed they breed them and novify them later, ala Inhumans? </div> </div> </div>Some baselines went with the Novas voluntarily most of the preAeon colonies were built by such. There are second and third generation Novas and possibly Aberrants at least in 1e though apparently they were less fertile than normal people generally but we don't know if that was transfered","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T22:28:56-08:00","id":1189530,"title":"","content":"Sounds more and more like The Eternals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T22:30:41-08:00","id":1189531,"title":"","content":"Do we know the status in the kids if Psions? I know they are new but they must be researching the next gen.<br /> <br /> <br /> If psions were made in Prometheus Chambers why were only the first made into Proxies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T05:03:34-08:00","id":1189576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1189531#post1189531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know the status in the kids if Psions? I know they are new but they must be researching the next gen.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are genetic markers for Latents so that's all we really know. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If psions were made in Prometheus Chambers why were only the first made into Proxies? </div> </div> </div>They started with more xp than everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T06:14:59-08:00","id":1189584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1189576#post1189576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They started with more xp than everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus I would not be surprised if the Setting Secrets chapter mentions why they started with more xp.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T12:01:59-08:00","id":1189648,"title":"","content":"This seems like a good a place as any to ask, a question I had even about 1e.<br /> After the Chinese ultimatum when all the Nova's left earth, did they supposedly just stop erupting? I would think there would still be new eruptions under the same circumstances, as there were before, what made them just 'go away' like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T12:17:11-08:00","id":1189655,"title":"","content":"Have you heard the term &quot;runaway greenhouse effect?&quot; The idea is that, as the climate gets warmer, the warming oceans and melting ice caps etc. cause more CO<sub>2</sub> to end up in the atmosphere, which causes more warming, which causes more CO<sub>2</sub> to be released, etc. Having too much of a thing past a certain &quot;tipping point&quot; causes more of that thing to happen.<br /> <br /> During the Nova Age, there's a lot of Quantum energies blanketing the Earth. A lot. Eruptions keep happening because there's still a lot of ambient Quantum.<br /> <br /> After the Chinese Ultimatum, almost all of that Quantum is suddenly gone. There's no more tipping point. People may or may not erupt again in the future, but (outside of QFZs) it's at normal rates, and not the rates we got during the Nova Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T13:58:07-08:00","id":1189684,"title":"","content":"Apropos of nothing, but do we know what the last phases of the OP Kickstarters usually look like? Do they close really strong? While I for sure want the Weapons stretch goal, I'm beyond excited for the Nihonjin Superiors. I pitched another bit in to that end but I'm curious if it's money well spent based on previous campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T22:51:42-08:00","id":1189787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Anne Country</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1189684#post1189684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apropos of nothing, but do we know what the last phases of the OP Kickstarters usually look like? Do they close really strong? While I for sure want the Weapons stretch goal, I'm beyond excited for the Nihonjin Superiors. I pitched another bit in to that end but I'm curious if it's money well spent based on previous campaigns.</div> </div> </div> </div>They close fairly strong; Superiors are certainly in expected range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T23:45:59-08:00","id":1189793,"title":"","content":"I'm still hoping that Psiads will be achieved. I'm not going to hold my breath, but I have hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T00:20:22-08:00","id":1189797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1189793#post1189793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still hoping that Psiads will be achieved. I'm not going to hold my breath, but I have hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and me both, on both counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T21:01:11-08:00","id":1190558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1189793#post1189793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still hoping that Psiads will be achieved. I'm not going to hold my breath, but I have hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll be there before dawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T22:04:39-08:00","id":1190566,"title":"","content":"Barring major pull outs, it's done <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's all gravy from here","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T22:08:32-08:00","id":1190568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1189648#post1189648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like a good a place as any to ask, a question I had even about 1e.<br /> After the Chinese ultimatum when all the Nova's left earth, did they supposedly just stop erupting? I would think there would still be new eruptions under the same circumstances, as there were before, what made them just 'go away' like that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In addition to the point Ian already made about the amount of Quantum bathing the earth when the Novas were active there resulting in tons more eruptions - also remember that Quantum and Psi inherently counter each other. So Nova eruptions would have plummeted immediately after the existent Novas left, but after Psions rise and Psi-Tech arrives, Eruptions would have gone from rare to virtually unheard of as the planet is bathed in Psi energy.<br /> <br /> (&quot;virtually&quot; being the most important word in that last sentence)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T14:03:27-07:00","id":1261640,"title":"","content":"One of the other difficulties that Trinity had was that it was the first of the gaming trilogy. As such its creation system bore a great resemblance to those of the Old World of Darkness (you get xx number of Attribute, Skill and Background point. You get three dots in psionic modes and then 15 Freebie points to customize your character with. The end result was somebody with distinct advantages over a vanilla human but far from invincible.<br /> <br /> Then Aberrant came out. It used the same basic system to build the human aspects of skills, attributes, etc but then added 30 Nova point which effectively turned the characters into near-gods compared to the Psions and Neutral human. The insane power creep didn't help matters (Universe Creation? Really? That's going to happen often enough to require a system for doing it?)<br /> <br /> The final game, Adventure, fell maybe halfway between Trinity and Aberrant but the &quot;transformed&quot; still came out far more flexible and capable than Psions did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-20T08:26:35-07:00","id":1261764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1261640#post1261640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Universe Creation? Really? That's going to happen often enough to require a system for doing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, 99% of the reason for Universe Creation seeing print was to set up the idea that that's why Divis Mal wasn't showing up in the Trinity books -- he'd decided &quot;screw all this,&quot; created his own universe, and moved there with those closest to him, never to return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T17:22:45-07:00","id":1262256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1261764#post1261764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, 99% of the reason for Universe Creation seeing print was to set up the idea that that's why Divis Mal wasn't showing up in the Trinity books -- he'd decided &quot;screw all this,&quot; created his own universe, and moved there with those closest to him, never to return.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then he got beaten up by Exalts and made into Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T18:30:00-07:00","id":1262448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1262256#post1262256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then he got beaten up by Exalts and made into Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually fits because Exalted takes places in the &quot;before times&quot; of the Old World of Darkness as I recall. So, Divis Mal created the World of Darkness. It works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T12:17:34-08:00","id":1268607,"title":"","content":"Eden\u2019s Novas are weaker because they don\u2019t push their powers and take the slow power climb that\u2019s also why they have little or no taint. They\u2019s also a short of stop in novas power levels if they are not willing to accept taint it\u2019s not a hard stop but only a few individuals get around it with out taint. The lack of taint is important for the Eden Novases because they believe that taint turns Novases into the monsters that the Aberrants have become","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T15:20:28-08:00","id":1268650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1268607#post1268607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eden\u2019s Novas are weaker because they don\u2019t push their powers and take the slow power climb that\u2019s also why they have little or no taint. They\u2019s also a short of stop in novas power levels if they are not willing to accept taint it\u2019s not a hard stop but only a few individuals get around it with out taint. The lack of taint is important for the Eden Novases because they believe that taint turns Novases into the monsters that the Aberrants have become</div> </div> </div> </div>Very Useful Info!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T15:42:15-08:00","id":1268654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1189655#post1189655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you heard the term &quot;runaway greenhouse effect?&quot; The idea is that, as the climate gets warmer, the warming oceans and melting ice caps etc. cause more CO<sub>2</sub> to end up in the atmosphere, which causes more warming, which causes more CO<sub>2</sub> to be released, etc. Having too much of a thing past a certain &quot;tipping point&quot; causes more of that thing to happen.<br /> <br /> During the Nova Age, there's a lot of Quantum energies blanketing the Earth. A lot. Eruptions keep happening because there's still a lot of ambient Quantum.<br /> <br /> After the Chinese Ultimatum, almost all of that Quantum is suddenly gone. There's no more tipping point. People may or may not erupt again in the future, but (outside of QFZs) it's at normal rates, and not the rates we got during the Nova Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>So does this mean Eden is overrun with new Novas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T22:16:10-08:00","id":1268726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1268607#post1268607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eden\u2019s Novas are weaker because they don\u2019t push their powers and take the slow power climb that\u2019s also why they have little or no taint. They\u2019s also a short of stop in novas power levels if they are not willing to accept taint it\u2019s not a hard stop but only a few individuals get around it with out taint. The lack of taint is important for the Eden Novases because they believe that taint turns Novases into the monsters that the Aberrants have become</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously haven\u2019t seen 2e Aberrant yet, but if Terragen Chrysalis is still a thing, it\u2019s possible that in the long run going all the way to Tier 4 Eximorph is actually Taint/shedding-humanity based, and not something that the Edenites, retaining their humanity, are capable of.<br /> <br /> Not that Tier 3 (the base tier for Novas, the tier Psymorphs achieve as Proxies, and that Maxwell Mercer stands alone on as a Paramorph) is anything to sneeze at!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T22:17:17-08:00","id":1268728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1268654#post1268654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So does this mean Eden is overrun with new Novas?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would mean in theory they have a rate of eruption in their human population comparable to the height of the Nova Age on Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T23:24:05-08:00","id":1268737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1268728#post1268728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would mean in theory they have a rate of eruption in their human population comparable to the height of the Nova Age on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could it be higher since they took the Nova population of a 7 billion person planet and condensed it to a few million human starting pop?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T23:38:33-08:00","id":1268740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1268737#post1268737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could it be higher since they took the Nova population of a 7 billion person planet and condensed it to a few million human starting pop?</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly could be, but I\u2019m operating under the assumption there\u2019s a ceiling. Only a certain percentage of the population is going to be CAPABLE of erupting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T00:00:55-08:00","id":1268745,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I didn\u2019t consider it could be the ceiling but that could work. Perhaps if you dip beyond that then taint is inevitable. <br /> <br /> Still would like them to consider handling the Nova fertility issues, I want my Inhuman Attilan or Eternals of Titan!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T01:57:21-08:00","id":1268763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1189336-are-\u00e6on-abberants-still-comparable-to-novas?p=1268737#post1268737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could it be higher since they took the Nova population of a 7 billion person planet and condensed it to a few million human starting pop?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... Where did you get this?<br /> <br /> Eden's got a human population of around 1.2 million, and there are about 60 novas altogether. While that's a higher proportion of novas to baselines than during the Nova Age, that's not anywhere near the entire nova population of Earth.<br /> <br /> I don't see the eruption rate being terribly high. During the Nova Age, Earth itself was blanketed with Quantum energies. Eden has a normal expected background rate of Flux energies.There are a bunch of novas in one place, which raises the Flux levels higher for the population centres, but it's not on par with what Earth had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T02:01:28-08:00","id":1268764,"title":"","content":"Not an expert on this setting thanks for the clarity!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}